cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use lcc in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "lcc: Local Context Compiler"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Lucas
    family-names: Martins
    affiliation: LookADev
version: "1.4.0"
date-released: "2026-11-07"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lucasmartins-ai/lcc"
url: "https://lucasmartins-ai.github.io/lcc/"
abstract: >-
  lcc compacts the context of AI coding agents on the local machine. Its verbatim stashed mode replaces
  bulky tool output with a pointer and keeps the exact bytes in a content-addressed stash that the agent
  can recall. The LongHealth v1 pre-registered study in benchmarks/research/longhealth-v1 measures it
  on public fictional clinical records.
keywords:
  - context compaction
  - large language models
  - coding agents
  - long context
